++++# Pipeline Position
++ +
++-+**Rules**
++++Single source of truth for how a play declares where it sits in the delivery pipeline and
++++what start/end machinery create-play folds into it. This is the D2 auto-build rule (#434):
++++the composition lives here once, so every play create-play compiles wires the same
++++start-change opening and the same commit → propose → review → merge closing — instead of
++++each play re-deciding how a change is opened and landed.
++ +
++-+- It is a destination: sources, capabilities, slices, its plan and its epics point at it. It points only at its capabilities, the business intents it was identified by and, loosely, its domains. It does not point at its slices; they are found from the slices' side.
++-+- It is the only kind with the label `product` in the tracker.
++-+- It holds no ICE, and Garura never works on it directly. Agents work on the ICE of its capabilities and of their features.
++-+- A work item reaches it through its Epic.
++-+- Each capability it has is linked both ways: the capability's spine entry names it in `intents`, and its Touches list names the capability with the mark. A play that makes one side writes the other.
++-+- It is met by its proof, never because its work is finished.
++-+- Work starts only from an ICE that is ready or partly ready. An ICE whose capability serves no confirmed business intent is kept, not worked on, and is drift for alignment, never a blocked write.
++-+- A source is never copied into it; the source shows the intent, it is not the intent.
++-+- It is written for a business reader, in plain words.
++-+- Only a person confirms or drops it; an agent never does.
++-+- Two intents that touch the same capability in opposite ways are a clash, shown to a person before work starts.
++-+- Business intents never need one another. They may be identified by one another — a connection, never a dependency; neither waits on the other. Plan files use it: for example, #722 is identified by #717.
++++It governs only the **delivery pipeline** (the path that opens an issue, does the work, and
++++lands it on main). Every play declares where it sits; many model-building plays now open and
++++land their own change. As compiled today: `both` — /discover-domains, /discover-capabilities (#616), /shape-measure-lens,
++++/shape-slice, /learn-outcomes, /fix-bug, /refactor-code, /discover-intent (#612), /record-decision (#632), /edit-ontology (#777 — a meta play that opens and lands its own change); `start` — /shape-architecture-lens, /shape-ux-lens, /build-epic; `end` —
++++/shape-marketing-lens, /shape-run-lens, /release-epic; `none` — /shape-agentic-lens, /shape-quality-lens, /validate-epic, /release-increment,
++++/list-focus-issues. (A `none` play runs on whatever branch is already started.) Inside a loop the
++++opening and the end sequence are both skipped — the loop opens and lands the change — and a
++++play knows it is inside a loop from the loop's contract (`standards/rules/loop-contract.md`;
++++ADR 029, ADR 030 P4). Wired so far: /discover-intent (#612, its own contract check), and /discover-domains (#614) and
++++/discover-capabilities (#615), both with the shared `check_loop_contract.py`.
++ +
++-+**States**
++++## The declaration
++ +
++-+proposed → confirmed (the person who asked confirms it says the right thing) → met (its proof holds). A proposed or confirmed intent can be dropped (a person drops it, with a reason).
++++Every play declares one frontmatter field:
++ +
++-+**Example**
++++```yaml
++++position: start | end | both | none
++++```
++ +
