+++++# No unbacked recommendation — the cardinal rule
++ ++
++-++The branch name says what the change is (start-change, #731):
+++++**Silence beats a wrong answer.** A play that recommends an action must be able to name
+++++the source that backs it. Where it cannot, it says nothing — it never fills the gap with a
+++++default, a generic pointer, or another play's name.
++ ++
++-++  plan/<P>/<issue>-<slug>   an issue in plan P   → lands on plan/<P>/base
++-++  plan/<P>/base             plan P itself        → lands on main, while the plan is still in
++-++                                                   progress (a plan merges when it pauses)
++-++  anything else             a one-off change     → lands on main
+++++Set on 2026-09-08 as a cardinal rule: it is better not to recommend when the source is not
+++++known than to recommend wrongly.
++ ++
++-++    python3 resolve_target.py --branch <branch> [--out <target.json>]
