+-+### 4. Only breaking main holds a plan's branch back
+++- `list` — one line for each plan: its branch, Done against open, what is worked now, the plans
+++  it waits on. Used by `/list-plans`.
+++- `show` — one plan as a tree, with the plans it needs after it. Done and Dropped are hidden and
+++  counted. Used by `/show-plan`.
+++- `graph` — each plan's branch against main, with commits ahead and behind. Used by
+++  `/list-plans --graph`.
+ +
+-+A plan's branch is never kept off main just because the plan is not done. The only reason to hold
+-+it back is that it would break main. The review (check-change) and the merge checks (approved, no
+-+conflicts, no failing required checks) decide that. Plan order (`needs_plans`) no longer holds a
+-+plan off main.
+++Every mark and line comes from the `plan-view.md` template (its ```yaml plan-view block). A play
+++gets the template from `template-manager` and passes the copy's path with `--template`.
+ +
+-+### 5. No detour plans
+++The six statuses of a plan's node are Not Started, In Progress, Now, Done, Blocked and Dropped.
+++A plan file with any other status is refused (exit 2), so an old file is never shown wrongly.
+ +
+-+A detour plan does not land back on the plan it came from. Pause the plan the detour came from
+-+(merge it into main), cut the detour from main, and land the detour on main. #791, which was to
+-+teach the change plays to land a detour back on its plan, is closed as not needed.
